<speak>
Chapter One. The lighthouse stood at the far edge of the island, and every evening its keeper climbed the iron stairs to light the lamp.
<break time="1500ms"/>
Chapter Two. In the morning the fog rolled in from the sea, and the fishing boats waited in the harbor for the bells to ring.
<break time="1500ms"/>
Chapter Three. Nobody remembered who had built the tower, only that it had always been there, patient and white against the cliffs.
<break time="1500ms"/>
Chapter Four. When the storm finally came, the keeper wrote one line in the logbook and went upstairs to wait.
</speak>
